Error [E0119]: there's no type called `View`
  --> tests/ui/view_outlives_owner.jet:1:14
    |
  1 | fn make() => View<Int> {
    |              ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: generic types must name a struct or enum you defined
 Fix: check the spelling, or define the type first

Error [E0119]: `View` isn't generic
  --> tests/ui/view_outlives_owner.jet:1:14
    |
  1 | fn make() => View<Int> {
    |              ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: only types declared with type parameters accept `<…>`
 Fix: use `View` without type arguments

Error [E2305]: this view points into `incidents`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/view_outlives_owner.jet:3:21
    |
  3 |     return incidents[0..2]
    |                     ^^^^^^
 Why: `incidents` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: return an owned copy with `~place` (for example `~value[a..b]`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it

